{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>לא ידון רוחי.</b> Some say it is like וישב חרבו אל נדנה (1 Chronicles 21:27), for the body is to the spirit like a sheath, and the proof is איתכרית רוחי (Daniel 7:15), only ידון would be from a different root, like \"אם יעלה לשמים שיאו\" (Job 20:6), which is from the root נחי, and like it are נשא and many others. And some say its pattern is like \"וישב העפר\" (Ecclesiastes 12:7), and it is from the root דין, for the spirit judges in the body." "<b>בשגם.</b> The shin is like the shin of שככה, and its meaning is: My spirit shall not endure, since it was from Him. And so Ecclesiastes says: \"והרוח תשוב אל האלהים אשר נתנה\" (Ecclesiastes 12:7). Rather, the spirit of man alone, because of this violence, and further because man is flesh, shall endure until a time and then cease, when that which is made is overcome by its maker." "\"And his days shall be\" — this is the measure for all mankind, and if we find more, we find but few; rather it speaks of the majority. And this is not true, for Shem lived six hundred years, and all the generations after him lived many years, and in the days of Peleg the years diminished, and from the days of David until today seventy or eighty years. And the truth is what the Aramaic translator [Onkelos] said, that He set a deadline for man, like the meaning of \"עוד ארבעים יום\" (Jonah 3:4) — if they repent they will be saved, and if they do not repent they will die. And do not set your mind on the number of \"ויהי נח בן חמש מאות שנה\" (Genesis 5:32), for there is no chronological order in the Torah. And leave aside \"וימת תרח בחרן\" (Genesis 11:32), followed by \"ויאמר ד׳ אל אברם לך לך מארצך\" (Genesis 12:1) — yet we know that Terah did not die until Isaac was thirty-five years old, and many like it."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {2 "Resolved המתרגם ארמית as Onkelos by inference from context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:32.081329434Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}